Python and uv

Install:
  Install missing uv and a uv-managed Python interpreter; create missing default Python command links.

Upgrade:
  Update installed uv and uv-managed Python versions.

Status:
  Report uv and Python command locations and versions; list locally detected Python installations.

Requirements:
  Ubuntu, APT and a regular user with sudo access.

Configuration:
  Missing uv is installed in ~/.local/bin; Python versions and command links use uv's configured directories.
  Install creates a uv-managed interpreter even when system Python is present; existing python/python3 entries in uv's command directory are preserved.
  Upgrade updates existing uv-managed Python versions and leaves system Python unchanged.
  CLI tools such as ruff and pre-commit belong to the tools module.
  Open a new terminal after installation to load environment changes.
